# .cursorrules — PSO Forecourt AI Surveillance (Pilot)
#
# Client: PSO Pump — 295-A, Airlines Society, Lahore · Vendor: M. Resolutions
# 1.5-month pilot on the client's EXISTING Dahua PTZ (8MP/4K) cameras. No new hardware.
#
# THE ONE RULE:
#   Get a CLEAR, READABLE image first — then build AI on top of it.
#   Sequence, strictly:
#     clear image → repeatable clear image → understand the scene → capture the right moments →
#     read them → connect them → prove it.
#
# GATES (execute in strict order, do not build ahead):
#   M0  Scaffold & rails                                  — runnable skeleton + /health + tests.
#   M1  Camera-control probe                              — capability matrix per camera model. GATE.
#   M2  Blur-free, human-verified capture                 — human can read meter + plate on stills. GATE.
#   M3  Repeatable sharp presets                          — presets return the same crisp view.
#   M4  RTSP ingest & baseline (reliability)              — reconnect on drop; day+night baseline.
#   M5  Detection & tracking                              — YOLO + ByteTrack, stable IDs, offline replay.
#   M6  Operational core (early wins)                     — zones/lines/dwell, after-hours, queue.
#   M7  Backend, storage & live dashboard                 — the screen staff use, true/false feedback.
#   M8  Choreographed capture sequencer                   — trigger → meter → plate → people (best-effort).
#   M9  Meter reading                                     — sale detected + amount, litres×rate self-check.
#   M10 Plate reading & sale↔vehicle link                 — the payoff: attribution + drive-off with amount.
#   M11 Prove, tune & pilot report                        — before/after review with real numbers.
#
# HOW THE AGENT WORKS:
# - ONE milestone at a time. Finish → test → demo → commit → next.
# - Every task ends with a test AND a runnable demo. No "trust me".
# - Keep it runnable OFFLINE on saved clips (`scripts/replay_clip.py`).
# - If blocked by missing input (RTSP URL, creds, GPU, real clip), STOP and ASK.
# - RESPECT THE GATES: no meter/plate OCR (M9-M10) until M1-M3 prove a human-readable capture.
# - Commit per milestone with the milestone number in the message (e.g. "M4: RTSP ingest + reconnect").
# - Update this file when an architectural decision changes.
#
# CODING STANDARDS:
# - Type hints everywhere; `ruff` + `mypy` clean; format with `ruff format`.
# - Small, single-responsibility modules; no 500-line files.
# - ALL tunables in `config/` — never hard-coded.
# - Every module ships tests.
# - Structured logging (camera id + track id + event on every alert); never print().
# - Graceful failure: dead camera logs + retries, never crashes the pipeline.
# - Secrets only via .env/environment. Dashboard: no browser localStorage/sessionStorage.
#
# STACK:
# - Python 3.11+, FastAPI, Ultralytics YOLO (v11), ByteTrack, Shapely, OpenCV/FFmpeg,
#   ONVIF (onvif-zeep) + Dahua HTTP API, SQLite (WAL), pydantic-settings, loguru,
#   React + Vite + TS + Tailwind, docker-compose, ONNX/TensorRT for deploy.
#
# See ROADMAP.md and each `src/<module>/README-ish docstring` for details.
